      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have done more testing and got a little more information. This is not a steam issue since this only happens with vrc desktop (vr mode uses virtual desktop audio drivers and there is no issues). I have uninstalled and reinstalled the realtek drivers, checked the built in BIOS for anything that stood out. It appears unity clashes with nahimic services and this is a common issue but when looking at windows services, there is no nahimic service installed at all so this potential solution does not work. Exclusive Mode is disabled (disabled during testing both did not work). I am running on Realtek Audio Driver Version 6.0.9239.1. If anyone has any potential solutions or at least something that would cause this issue, that would be most appreciated! If anyone needs any additional information as well, please let me know! ^_^",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
